1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,320
This system from XPeng is definitely
comparable to Tesla FSD Supervised.

2
00:00:04,320 --> 00:00:07,000
XPeng NGP. Nice.

3
00:00:17,440 --> 00:00:21,600
Good job. There are people in the lane
and we're moving through.

4
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:27,200
Not one weird thing, for how packed
and busy this street is.

5
00:00:27,200 --> 00:00:32,800
People are waving us through, thanking us
- and it was the car letting them through.

6
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:38,640
Very impressed by the performance in the
construction sites.

7
00:00:38,640 --> 00:00:42,640
The car is really confident with the
autonomous driving.

8
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:47,200
NGP doesn't keep stop-starting, halting.

9
00:00:47,200 --> 00:00:52,880
The drive is very smooth, and it deals
with different scenarios really well.

10
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:58,000
My only experience with self-driving is
Tesla FSD back home - NGP did amazing.

11
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:03,280
People on the roads, bikes everywhere,
and at no point did the car hesitate.

12
00:01:03,280 --> 00:01:09,040
Against Tesla Full Self-Driving, this
stands out: it is just rock solid.

13
00:01:09,040 --> 00:01:12,080
It recognises police vehicles and
visualises them on the screen.

14
00:01:12,080 --> 00:01:17,440
It shows centimetre-level differences
between me and the car we're approaching.

15
00:01:17,440 --> 00:01:20,480
You can see this being the leading
driver assistance in Europe.

16
00:01:20,480 --> 00:01:24,000
You're here in Paris, and the traffic
is tough.

17
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:32,320
People walking at the side, traffic,
buildings blocking the road -

18
00:01:32,320 --> 00:01:40,640
and it navigated so easily, with
technology that anticipates traffic.

19
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:48,880
I've driven German cars all my life.
First time with Chinese cars - impressed.

20
00:01:48,880 --> 00:01:57,410
I know Tesla FSD Supervised well, and in
Europe only two players can do this.

21
00:02:00,400 --> 00:02:07,550
A lady was crossing. Rather than braking
next to her, it saw her, slowed while

22
00:02:07,550 --> 00:02:13,920
she crossed, and pulled away once
she was clear.

23
00:02:13,920 --> 00:02:22,310
XPeng builds to UN DCAS regulations,
so the system can work everywhere.

24
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:27,440
How it responds, how it reacts,
how it anticipates.

25
00:02:27,440 --> 00:02:31,680
All of that makes it very comfortable.

26
00:02:31,680 --> 00:02:38,940
You don't have to focus on the chaotic
traffic and the foreign driving patterns.

27
00:02:40,720 --> 00:02:46,560
A very human-like drive - even better
than a human driver.

28
00:02:46,560 --> 00:02:54,400
The NGP feels more calculated: it sees
more of what's around it, a full 360.

29
00:02:54,400 --> 00:03:03,540
This could get ordinary people
considering full self-driving next time.

30
00:03:04,800 --> 00:03:13,200
Almost a chicane of people crossing, and
it saw all of it and went through.

31
00:03:13,200 --> 00:03:21,920
Almost as if the car knew what would
happen - that shows my confidence in it.

32
00:03:21,920 --> 00:03:28,080
Paris is a messy city: traffic, bicycles,
a lot going on.

33
00:03:28,080 --> 00:03:30,480
And it handled everything well.

34
00:03:30,480 --> 00:03:37,520
A polite driver inside the city, reading
its surroundings and behaving accordingly.

35
00:03:37,520 --> 00:03:43,040
One thing to highlight: its interactions
with pedestrians all around.

36
00:03:43,040 --> 00:03:50,560
It knew whether they were stopping to load
a car or crossing, with oncoming traffic.

37
00:03:50,560 --> 00:03:55,680
XPeng and Tesla are the two at the show
because they lead in this technology.

38
00:03:55,680 --> 00:03:59,200
It will revolutionise how we see
transportation.

39
00:03:59,200 --> 00:04:06,240
Very strong - in some moments better
than I think version 14 would have been.

40
00:04:06,240 --> 00:04:16,160
If you're in the market in Europe,
I'd encourage you to test drive this car.
